    "created_at": "2026-02-11T10:47:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-02-11T10:47:36Z",
    "body": "Chromium copies the `click` event's `bubbles` when creating the `DOMActivate` event. WebKit and Gecko seemingly always set `bubbles` to true.\n\nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/dom/node.cc;l=3280-3285\n\nhttps://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/14515\n\nOther things to test:\n\n- cancelling\n- default action handling\n  - differences between `el.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent(\"click\"))`, `el.dispatchEvent(new Event(\"DOMActivate\"))`, `el.click()` (see [this comment](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/forms/html_input_element.cc;l=1532-1534?q=DOMActivate&ss=chromium%2Fchromium%2Fsrc:third_party%2Fblink%2Frenderer%2Fcore%2Fhtml%2Fforms%2F&start=11))\n  - transient user activation for things that open a picker\n- legacy-pre-activation behavior and legacy-canceled-activation behavior for `<input type=checkbox>` and `radio`\n- behavior for disabled form controls\n- Gecko: `ShouldPreventDOMActivateDispatch()` special-cases `<input type=file>` internal button\n- guard against re-entrant/double DOMActivate\n- `trusted` when the `click` event has `trusted = false`\n- `composed`\n- event path if the node is disconnected or crosses shadow boundary\n- command/commandfor\n- popover",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
